<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Gunmen kills six in Krakow, three more bodies found at his house</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01e1e6dc4029a05ec86f1201f3ec3186392a4f81b049669d7fd05f0945f00e76</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T22:47:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gunmen-kills-six-in-krakow-three-more-bodies-found-at-his-house--dc06bdec4f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gunmen-kills-six-in-krakow-three-more-bodies-found-at-his-house" /><summary type="html">A chilling new discovery in Poland, where three bodies have reportedly been found inside the Krakow gunman's home. That's in addition to six people killed and sixteen wounded when the attacker opened fire in the city's historic square. Prime Minister Donald Tusk has now declared the shooting an act of terrorism, saying Poland has never experienced anything quite like it. The 25-year-old suspect, described by authorities as holding radical far-right views, was shot by police.</summary></entry><entry><title>'A violent fighter and warrior': Trump offers press secretary role to UFC chief Dana White</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8fea2af546eca41882948053862a10356a0f0022a1e41a64997b1a7d988dfb2</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T20:45:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-a-violent-fighter-and-warrior-trump-offers-press-secretary-role-to-ufc-chief-dana-white--b52c016d4787.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-a-violent-fighter-and-warrior-trump-offers-press-secretary-role-to-ufc-chief-dana-white" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday said he was asking mixed martial arts promoter Dana White to be the new White House press secretary. Trump has repeatedly tried to hitch his MAGA brand of politics to White's enormously successful Ultimate Fighting Championship.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>France Unbowed’s Mélenchon unveils ‘A Shared Future’ manifesto ahead of 2027 presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:680443e641312e42e66ab6606ebfd8918b02e7212d4cd8a048afabaf0a45abb5</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:58:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261107-france-unbowed-s-m_lenchon-unveils-a-shared-future-manifesto-ahead-of-2027-presidential-rac--8b526a1069d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261107-france-unbowed-s-m%C3%A9lenchon-unveils-a-shared-future-manifesto-ahead-of-2027-presidential-race" /><summary type="html">“We are facing a crisis of human civilisation. And we are going to win.”
 
A defiant Jean-Luc Mélenchon was in fighting mood today as he presented his presidential manifesto at Le Bourget, north of Paris. 
 
It is his fourth bid for the French presidency, and he has chosen a venue steeped in left-wing campaign history: the site of François Hollande's famous 2012 rally.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Israeli president picks Netanyahu's rival Eisenkot to try to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e062d28def073a6aa444d2c972259f7eb2fa8973ea0472d51116e1c5a983830b</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:38:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government--bea9f93a0c67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli president picks Netanyahu's rival Eisenkot to try to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:488bb869a0f657a42037f0cd633a178c68fb66fe79005b7757d6b230f778d0d2</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:37:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government--bea9f93a0c67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog picked former military chief Gadi Eisenkot to try to form a government, he said in a statement Saturday. Last month's parliamentary elections left neither Eisenkot nor Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu with a clear path to building a majority.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'We must change everything': French far-left leader Mélenchon launches presidential programme</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63965c9d73deb19018a510f86fa571b58e0ab8c03dbd2efa7eddfc57713b5564</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T17:30:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261107-we-must-change-everything-french-far-left-leader-m_lenchon-launches-presidential-programme--0c144202df78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261107-we-must-change-everything-french-far-left-leader-m%C3%A9lenchon-launches-presidential-programme" /><summary type="html">Veteran leftist Jean-Luc Mélenchon formally announced his plan to raise France's minimum wage, cap prices for essential foods and restore the country's retirement age to 60 in a speech launching his 2027 presidential election programme on Saturday. Polls currently indicate that he is the left wing's strongest contender against far-right candidate Marine Le Pen.</summary></entry><entry><title>France investigating if bogus bomb threats against airlines linked to 'foreign powers'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63866d7b6e3526c1d568f522c08c2deb2125b43e706f46944460e11cc14f85f2</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T16:33:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-france-investigating-if-bogus-bomb-threats-against-airlines-linked-to-foreign-powers--a1fba242825f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-france-investigating-if-bogus-bomb-threats-against-airlines-linked-to-foreign-powers" /><summary type="html">French prosecutors are investigating a series of fake bomb threats that targeted commercial flights in Europe this week, including trying to establish whether foreign powers may be involved. Those responsible for the bogus threats have not been identified.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Paraguay’s impeached president charged over bank collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b760745bda1ef323adee7736ac155918a3b64854ba97ea5b6b6f101a1c02b6b</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T15:49:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-paraguay-s-impeached-president-charged-over-bank-collapse--b833d29e01a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-paraguay-s-impeached-president-charged-over-bank-collapse" /><summary type="html">Paraguay’s impeached president Santiago Pena was on Saturday charged over his business links to a major online bank whose sudden collapse has locked millions of people out of their money and sparked angry protests.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 At least five people killed in shooting in Krakow, Polish police say ⤵️</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e9d4b692f1c3f144edbc40d95d510536c196c3578937ddd90e2df2239c94367</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T15:26:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-at-least-three-people-killed-shooting-in-polish-city-of-krakow-police-say--f51ffab85332.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-at-least-three-people-killed-shooting-in-polish-city-of-krakow-police-say" /></entry><entry><title>Gunman who killed at least six people in Krakow had ‘far-right’ views, Polish government says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e43150e9a3680729eae1b0842832e299abf77d64f53aadb27a53cb0a899e1c4</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T15:23:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-at-least-three-people-killed-shooting-in-polish-city-of-krakow-police-say--f51ffab85332.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-at-least-three-people-killed-shooting-in-polish-city-of-krakow-police-say" /><summary type="html">A gunman reportedly "fascinated by far-right ideologies" shot and killed at least six people and wounded more than a dozen more in Krakow’s main market square on Saturday, Polish authorities said. Three more bodies were later found at the home of the gunman, who was wounded and taken into custody.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo calls on Uruguay's Catholics to be 'bridge builders'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9a9a47860589144465bfaf397e83944b56c0c784b0fa811d154b3f4296595ea</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:59:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-calls-on-uruguay-catholics-bridge-builders--ca30f16639ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-calls-on-uruguay-catholics-bridge-builders" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV urged Catholics in Uruguay to build bridges of faith and fraternity on the second day of his 12-day tour of Uruguay, Argentina and Peru. The pope's three-country tour comes just three weeks after he underwent surgery for lung cancer.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'We must change everything,' French far-left presidential candidate Mélenchon says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67d033d6a83c9749927f11d29e5f644f81eac660dd09734094feab8e2ece5389</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:44:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-french-presidential-hopeful-m_lenchon-launches-campaign-by-vowing-lower-retirement-age--b95f6b426650.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-french-presidential-hopeful-m%C3%A9lenchon-launches-campaign-by-vowing-lower-retirement-age" /><summary type="html">Veteran leftist Jean-Luc Mélenchon formally announced his plan to raise France's minimum wage, cap prices for essential foods and restore the country's retirement age to 60 in a speech launching his 2027 presidential election programme on Saturday. Polls currently indicate that he is the left wing's strongest contender against far-right candidate Marine Le Pen.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France braces for more nationwide protests as Yellow Vests urge 'mass disobedience'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cffcc6c002d4563f6b0cd5f6026fb3be3f5adaaee6f3c64d75d8e92fb439398b</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T13:29:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-braces-for-more-nationwide-protests-as-yellow-vests-urge-mass-disobedience--294946423bc1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-braces-for-more-nationwide-protests-as-yellow-vests-urge-mass-disobedience" /><summary type="html">French unions and student groups are set to take to the streets for another day of protests on Saturday, while the Yellow Vests movement plans a separate rally in central Paris despite a ban by authorities. The demonstrations follow weeks of youth-led unrest and nationwide strikes that drew hundreds of thousands of workers protesting over the rising cost of living. Paul Smith, Associate Professor in French history and politics at the University of Nottingham, and James André, France 24 reporter at Place de la République, share further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nations League: Zinedine Zidane balances surprise and continuity in his second roster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:094511272b9b4c49a16432654bd19003a5071115000fa3f39340e2de519536aa</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T13:27:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nations-league-zinedine-zidane-balances-surprise-and-continuity-in-his-second-roster--59f0dc28329b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nations-league-zinedine-zidane-balances-surprise-and-continuity-in-his-second-roster" /><summary type="html">Zinedine Zidane has unveiled his France squad for the upcoming Nations League clashes against Italy and Turkey. Pablo Pagis earns a surprise first call-up, while Kylian Mbappé and several other key players return from injury</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Banking scandal topples Paraguay leader</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a30905da8fe58b2b4ac050b815d43c9b85676da3eeeab20bcb3297cbe168f68c</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:16:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/banking-scandal-topples-paraguay-leader--780283ad5424.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/banking-scandal-topples-paraguay-leader" /><summary type="html">Paraguay’s ousted president Santiago Peña has been placed under house arrest after senators unanimously voted to remove him over a banking scandal. The collapse of Ueno Bank left nearly three million customers unable to access their savings. Peña denies any wrongdoing, while his successor, Pedro Alliana, has pledged to compensate those affected.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia launches massive strike on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81a50d024bedc777e31917c25078079158a3f7fd289ff10eedaefd71d86e1595</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:15:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261107-russia-launches-massive-strike-on-kyiv-1--1213cd3ff896.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261107-russia-launches-massive-strike-on-kyiv-1" /><summary type="html">As Ukraine prepares for another round of talks with Russia and the United States next week, Moscow has launched a massive overnight strike. At least five people were injured in Kyiv, where Russian missiles damaged residential and commercial buildings, forced the closure of a bridge over the Dnipro River and caused fresh power and water outages. Ophélie Jacobson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Stephen Miller named White House Chief of Staff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b36d1abb9e510f9255441ab85713077b595985f4b760df30c9b7373c52ce80e</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:14:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/stephen-miller-named-white-house-chief-of-staff--7469c4aafa30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/stephen-miller-named-white-house-chief-of-staff" /><summary type="html">Following historic Republican losses in the midterm elections, Donald Trump has replaced his chief of staff, Susie Wiles, with her deputy Stephen Miller, the architect of his administration’s immigration crackdown. Wiles had been seen by some as a stabilising force in the White House, but with Democrats now controlling both chambers of Congress, Trump is reportedly seeking a more aggressive approach to pushing his agenda. Caroline Baum reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel coalition talks gain momentum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98e0f2c29047a246aa46488bbe182a3536464f8c158aaa95ff75050c42636b71</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:12:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-coalition-talks-gain-momentum--e112145ab913.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-coalition-talks-gain-momentum" /><summary type="html">Following inconclusive elections in Israel, opposition candidate Gadi Eisenkot says he is confident of securing the mandate to form a government, as President Isaac Herzog prepares to nominate the first candidate. Eisenkot claims he is making progress in efforts to oust long-serving Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenyan cult leader sentenced to 200 years in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3aced97ac8df6304304bcf9fff8b33968aa798acce13626ff3106e72dcd60f54</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:10:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison-1--17cc7592b605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison-1" /><summary type="html">Kenyan cult leader Paul Mackenzie has been sentenced to 200 years in prison for the deaths of 190 children who were starved to death on his orders in Shakahola Forest. Prosecutors said he had convinced followers to fast to reach heaven before the apocalypse, with some victims beaten, buried alive or dumped in latrines. Twenty-eight accomplices have also been jailed. The case has raised serious questions about the authorities' failure to act on repeated warning signs dating back to 2017, with the death toll from the wider investigation reaching 448 confirmed bodies and around 500 suspected victims.</summary></entry><entry><title>Retired tennis star Gaël Monfils named captain of France's Davis Cup team</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53436f96ef46e8c013aaadae0894b6db8239fc0746c442ea45631da937c13e84</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:07:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-retired-tennis-star-ga_l-monfils-named-captain-of-france-s-davis-cup-team--90c453f0afbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-retired-tennis-star-ga%C3%ABl-monfils-named-captain-of-france-s-davis-cup-team" /><summary type="html">Recently retired tennis player Gaël Monfils was named captain of the French Davis Cup team, the country's tennis federation announced Saturday. France will next take part in the Davis Cup in February 2027 after having failed to qualify for this year's finals in Bologna.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>French presidential election: How far-left Mélenchon became a Gen Z favourite</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac2d02c9e0a04cc9f62667ce1f604ad55c0cafa44b744ffae0a15108212e2bd2</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T10:44:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-french-2027-presidential-elections-how-m_lenchon-became-a-gen-z-favourite--88c7b198e33d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-french-2027-presidential-elections-how-m%C3%A9lenchon-became-a-gen-z-favourite" /><summary type="html">Far-left presidential candidate Jean-Luc Mélenchon presents his policy platform at a key rally near Paris on Saturday. A polarising figure for the general electorate, he is nonetheless beloved among France's youth, who are drawn to his progressive policy proposals and say he empowers them to get more involved in politics.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Pope urges healthcare for all in Uruguay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f84fe7e68700b48680c3686d86ae0be16d9f1d4155b7d3d90ed999cf25a0248</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:41:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/pope-urges-healthcare-for-all-in-uruguay--cc244f5a7f44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pope-urges-healthcare-for-all-in-uruguay" /><summary type="html">Three weeks after undergoing surgery for lung cancer, Pope Francis has begun a three-nation tour of Latin America, saying he felt better than he looked. His first stop is Uruguay, the continent’s most secular country. Jack Pownall reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI Data centres face growing backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e2331be5c9bf774f5bc8a142ca584b2b6f1c6dec4ef60f9583e1418f4cf9ab9</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:39:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ai-data-centres-face-growing-backlash--009b8f3b4c3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ai-data-centres-face-growing-backlash" /><summary type="html">Democrats are also calling for tighter regulation of AI data centres, a concern shared across Europe. In Amsterdam, several hundred activists occupied the site of a planned Microsoft data centre as part of a two-day protest taking place across the continent. Jennie Shin reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: 30 dead in strikes on Taiz market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c907417c557640401f1b6d7c60c17119f6ee5de33a934e559e66e9d5283275e2</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:37:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-30-dead-in-strikes-on-taiz-market--556471887193.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-30-dead-in-strikes-on-taiz-market" /><summary type="html">At least 30 people have reportedly been killed in an attack on a market in Yemen’s Taiz province, with Houthi rebels blaming Saudi airstrikes. Government forces and local authorities have disputed the claim, instead accusing the Houthis of indiscriminate fire. The province has witnessed intense clashes in recent weeks and is home to around half of the more than 300,000 people displaced by the latest fighting. Caroline Baum reports.</summary></entry></feed>
